# Unshift inserts one value before the first element

Verifies unshift places each value in front of the elements already stored,
so successive insertions end up in front of one another in the printed array.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [30, 40]
values->unshift(20)
values->unshift(10)
print(values)

<<< stdout
[10, 20, 30, 40]

<<< stderr
